---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Screen Sharing Remote"
  description="Screen Sharing Remote collects no data. No account, no analytics, no servers."
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 10, 2026</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Screen Sharing Remote collects nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising,
      and no server operated by us.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app does with data</h2>
    <p>
      The app connects your iPhone directly to a Mac you choose, over Apple's Screen Sharing
      protocol, on your own network. Screen contents, input events, and credentials travel
      between your devices only. We never see them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Connection settings, such as saved computers and session preferences, are stored on your
      device. If you delete the app, they are gone.
    </p>

    <h2>Permissions</h2>
    <p>
      The app asks for local network access to find and reach your Macs. It uses that access
      only to connect to the computers you pick.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      There are none. The app contains no third-party SDKs, trackers, or analytics frameworks.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions? Open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/iherdt/screen-sharing-remote">GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to Screen Sharing Remote</a></p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 20px 80px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 26px 0 8px;
  }
  p {
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .back {
    margin-top: 36px;
  }
</style>
